Figure 6 illustrates how Nano-11 enhances antigen targeting to immunopotentiating cells in the draining lymph node and improves antigen retention at the injection site. Panel A shows that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) express the highest levels of CD86, a key costimulatory molecule. Panel B further characterizes OVA-positive and OVA-negative MigDCs, detailing their CD11b and Ly6C expression. Panel C, using in vivo fluorescence imaging, demonstrates that Nano-11, like aluminum hydroxide, significantly prolongs antigen retention at the injection site over several days compared to soluble antigen, which clears rapidly. This sustained retention and targeting to MigDCs are crucial for Nano-11's adjuvant effect.